Per creare un'app per tracciare i libri che leggi con un backend FastAPI e SQLite, e un frontend React + Vite, segui questi passaggi:

1. **Inizializza il progetto backend FastAPI:**

```bash
mkdir backend
cd backend
python -m venv venv
source venv/bin/activate
pip install fastapi uvicorn sqlalchemy sqlite3
```

2. **Crea il file `main.py` per il backend FastAPI:**

```python
from fastapi import FastAPI, HTTPException
from pydantic import BaseModel
from sqlalchemy import create_engine, Column, Integer, String
from sqlalchemy.ext.declarative import declarative_base
from sqlalchemy.orm import sessionmaker

app = FastAPI()

DATABASE_URL = "sqlite:///./books.db"
engine = create_engine(DATABASE_URL, connect_args={"check_same_thread": False})
SessionLocal = sessionmaker(autocommit=False, autoflush=False, bind=engine)
Base = declarative_base()

class Book(Base):
    __tablename__ = "books"
    id = Column(Integer, primary_key=True, index=True)
    title = Column(String, index=True)
    author = Column(String, index=True)
    status = Column(String, index=True)

Base.metadata.create_all(bind=engine)

class BookCreate(BaseModel):
    title: str
    author: str
    status: str

class BookUpdate(BaseModel):
    status: str

def get_db():
    db = SessionLocal()
    try:
        yield db
    finally:
        db.close()

@app.post("/books/", response_model=Book)
def create_book(book: BookCreate, db: SessionLocal = get_db()):
    db_book = Book(title=book.title, author=book.author, status=book.status)
    db.add(db_book)
    db.commit()
    db.refresh(db_book)
    return db_book

@app.get("/books/", response_model=list[Book])
def read_books(db: SessionLocal = get_db()):
    books = db.query(Book).all()
    return books

@app.put("/books/{book_id}", response_model=Book)
def update_book(book_id: int, book: BookUpdate, db: SessionLocal = get_db()):
    db_book = db.query(Book).filter(Book.id == book_id).first()
    if not db_book:
        raise HTTPException(status_code=404, detail="Book not found")
    db_book.status = book.status
    db.commit()
    db.refresh(db_book)
    return db_book
```

3. **Avvia il backend FastAPI:**

```bash
uvicorn main:app --reload
```

4. **Inizializza il progetto frontend React + Vite:**

```bash
cd ..
npx create-vite@latest frontend --template react
cd frontend
npm install
```

5. **Crea il file `App.js` per il frontend React:**

```jsx
import React, { useState, useEffect } from 'react';
import axios from 'axios';

function App() {
  const [books, setBooks] = useState([]);
  const [title, setTitle] = useState('');
  const [author, setAuthor] = useState('');
  const [status, setStatus] = useState('to-read');

  useEffect(() => {
    fetchBooks();
  }, []);

  const fetchBooks = async () => {
    const response = await axios.get('http://127.0.0.1:8000/books/');
    setBooks(response.data);
  };

  const addBook = async () => {
    await axios.post('http://127.0.0.1:8000/books/', { title, author, status });
    fetchBooks();
    setTitle('');
    setAuthor('');
    setStatus('to-read');
  };

  const updateBookStatus = async (id, newStatus) => {
    await axios.put(`http://127.0.0.1:8000/books/${id}/`, { status: newStatus });
    fetchBooks();
  };

  return (
    <div>
      <h1>Book Tracker</h1>
      <div>
        <input type="text" placeholder="Title" value={title} onChange={(e) => setTitle(e.target.value)} />
        <input type="text" placeholder="Author" value={author} onChange={(e) => setAuthor(e.target.value)} />
        <select value={status} onChange={(e) => setStatus(e.target.value)}>
          <option value="to-read">To Read</option>
          <option value="reading">Reading</option>
          <option value="done">Done</option>
        </select>
        <button onClick={addBook}>Add Book</button>
      </div>
      <ul>
        {books.map((book) => (
          <li key={book.id}>
            {book.title} by {book.author} - {book.status}
            <button onClick={() => updateBookStatus(book.id, 'to-read')}>To Read</button>
            <button onClick={() => updateBookStatus(book.id, 'reading')}>Reading</button>
            <button onClick={() => updateBookStatus(book.id, 'done')}>Done</button>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>
    </div>
  );
}

export default App;
```

6. **Avvia il frontend React:**

```bash
npm run dev
```

Ora hai un'app completa per tracciare i libri che leggi, con un backend FastAPI e SQLite, e un frontend React + Vite.
